 them about their  own financial plans and their  investments and what they're doing it's  it's nothing they have no plan if their  business goes away they're completely  out of luck they're completely screwed  and so you need to start having that  financial plan so that you don't end up  with a major loss or being 60 and having  nothing to fall back on  i think it's important to get started  now so here's how i do it  when i'm looking at my projects i want  to spend 40  as a maximum on operations so everything  is based off of revenue  and this this video is going to get a  little more technical than i usually do  so let me know if you like it  uh in the comments below when i'm  looking at my budgeting  nina and i look at this every every  month so nina's in charge of my  operations  she's in charge of all the bank accounts  she's in charge of all the payments  she keeps a tight chip running when i  look at my  revenue numbers my operational budget  is 40 of revenue so to make this  video right to make my youtube channel  happen  uh for my editing team for my research  team for my thumbnail team  for my gear for you know my salary all  of that stuff  has to be 40 max of the revenue  and so at the beginning if it's just you  then  then don't start spending too far ahead  of the curve right i hate spending money  until i'm making money so these numbers  can still apply you can come up with  your own version of it  but the numbers still apply no matter  how much revenue you're making  you just stop spending more than you're  making that's like a that's a great  start at the beginning so many  entrepreneurs are looking for ways to  spend money  stop spending money until you're making  money that's that's the first great  bit of financial advice i would put in  and still do for a new project  i put in my time my energy my hustle my  heart but not my money  until i'm making money so once you're  making the money even a little bit of  money you're making 100 bucks  right 40 goes towards operations so you  got to buy  a camera and the camera cost you 100  bucks  that's a pretty cheap camera but still  whatever then you have to wait till you  have 400 bucks in revenue  right so you have your revenue and then  40 goes to operations at least for me  you can you can adjust these numbers for  your own business  25 for me goes to  advertising marketing uh any promotional  expenses  so that would also uh include travel in  the past  i'm not traveling right now because of  kovid but that would include my travel  that would include  any conferences that i was going to  where i wasn't getting paid to go and i  had to cover my own flight  and my own hotel so anything that's  related to advertising to marketing  that would be within 25 so i have a i  have an advertising budget  and this was actually hard for me to  start spending money  as my business group because i was so  i'm still in the mindset of i'm the  entrepreneur who  ate beans for lunch every day because i  was making 300 bucks a month  and so the idea of spending thousands  and thousands of dollars  on marketing uh  every day is it seems crazy  it seems crazy anyway i had to get over  it i still struggle with it but we're  getting there  so having the budget helps me right  having the budget  to spend money helps me so 40  is operations 25  is advertising marketing 10 is savings  so we take 10 of whatever whatever i  made whatever the cash flow was coming  in and we put that away and so that's  where then i'm investing that's the  tony robbins compounding strategy i  invest half of it into an index fund  that tracks the canadian stock market so  half of my money just basically tracks  the canadian stock market  the fees are super low on it and it's a  way better return than you'll get on a  mutual fund  and then the other half right now is  mixed between  facebook and amazon so i'll take  more of a flyer on half the money and  then the other half will be  much more safe just put into an index  fund so ten percent of whatever i make  in the business goes towards savings and  investments  five percent goes towards giving away  so my wife nina also loves to help and  loves to support other people  just just like i do and in my book built  to serve i talked about  one of the biggest things i missed when  i was looking through  what makes nina happy is being able to  to help other people  uh and and donate the causes so we  created a fund  where five percent of what we make goes  towards helping people  and she gets to pick that might be a  charity  that might be a dog rescue that might be  someone in her family  that might be you know supporting  somebody that she knows that might be  somebody's going through a hard time and  she's going to help them out that might  be  contributing to the education fund of  her nieces or nephews like  that changes every month so every month  we get a budget  five percent of whatever we make goes  towards supporting the people in our  lives and she gets uh  she gets to be in charge of that we just  make sure that it adds up to  a max of five percent and that's great  again we weren't doing enough of that in  the past  and five percent may not seem like a big  number but  even if you're making a thousand bucks  and you spend 50 bucks on somebody  by giving it makes you feel  more full it makes you feel more  energetic more optimistic more positive  more happy  and 50 bucks is enough you know 50 bucks  would make a big difference for somebody  if somebody helped you in your business  in your life  and you you get five people ten dollar  gift cards  with a with a handwritten note to say  thank you that can make a big difference  that'll make you feel really good  and that energy will translate into more  growth  in your life and in your business so  having that five percent especially for  nina i'm  i i give my time i give my time so i'll  speak at events for free i'll coach  people for free  i like to give my time that's my giving  nina is finding ways to give  our money and she gets to pick causes  that are important to her so it's very  rarely  kind of entrepreneurial causes it's more  charities that are close to her or  family or friends or people in our lives  that  that she just wants to help so  40 towards operations 25 towards  uh marketing advertising ten percent  toward savings  five percent towards helping other  people  and then the rest is towards new  projects so if i'm if i'm launching  something new  and i want to put some investment in  this is another one that's been  difficult for me to overcome because  again i hate spending money totally  making money  and so now we're at the point where my  time is more valuable than my money  at the beginning it was the flip at the  beginning i'm making 300 bucks a month i  have no money  uh it's just really hard and so i'm just  putting all of my time my time my time  my time my time in  now the time becomes a lot more valuable  and and so i'm  spending a little bit ahead of the curve  and again having that budget  helps me do it for me pulling 10 aside  to save was the easiest part  the spending on the sales and marketing  the spending on the operations the  spending on the new project suspending  on the giving away  was the thing i needed more help with  and as i do those things it allows me to  get more of the results that i want and  so  that's my financial plan as of right now  and we'll make some tweaks and some  changes and and  minor adjustments along the way but it's  super important that you have one  and even if you're again making 500  bucks a month  a thousand bucks a month 2 000 bucks a  month  that the percentages can still apply  because when you can say hey i'm only  going to spend  40 of my revenue on operations  it forces you to be more resourceful  people complain about  lack of resources i don't have enough  money to do what i want to do  i don't have enough team members to do  what i want to do and 